# Staging-first Studio & Builder

## Temporary override (2026-07-28 through 2026-07-30 inclusive)

**No staging-first for this window.** Studio / Builder / suite deploy default is **prod only**:

- Work and commit on **`main`**, push `origin main`, wait for CI SHA tags, roll out on Vyom **`.249`** (`indobase.in`) per `.cursor/rules/indobase-prod-redeploy.mdc`.
- Do **not** default to `staging` → `indobase.fun` / Hostinger for these deploys.
- Still: SHA image tags (not `:latest`), no force-push, explicit user ask before commit/push/deploy.

From **2026-07-31**, delete or ignore this override and follow the permanent staging-first workflow below.

---

## Branches

| Branch | Environment | Hosts |
|--------|-------------|--------|
| **`staging`** | Staging | `studio.indobase.fun`, `builder.indobase.fun` (Hostinger `72.61.242.251`) |
| **`main`** | Production | `studio.indobase.in`, `builder.indobase.in` (Vyom `.249`) |

Shared prod data plane stays on Vyom (`api.indobase.in`, `*.indobase.in` tenants) for both.

## Default workflow (Studio / Builder / control-plane)

1. Work and **commit on `staging`** (create/checkout if needed). Do **not** commit Studio/Builder changes to `main` by default.
2. When asked to push/deploy staging: `git push origin staging`, wait for CI images, roll out with `IMAGE_TAG=<sha> ./docker/scripts/deploy-staging-hostinger.sh`.
3. Smoke on `*.indobase.fun` before any prod talk.
4. Only when the user explicitly asks to **promote / ship to prod / deploy to Vyom**: merge or cherry-pick into `main`, push `origin main`, then follow the production redeploy rule (Vyom `.249`).

## Do not

- Push Studio/Builder fixes straight to `main` or Vyom while staging is untested.
- Treat “deploy” as prod by default — prefer staging unless they say prod/Vyom/`indobase.in`.
- Force-push `staging` or `main` unless explicitly requested.

